@prefix shacl: <https://vng.nl/shacl/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

shacl:ValidateModelBBoxes a shacl:Shape ;
    shacl:id "ValidateModelBBoxes" ;
    shacl:description """
This SHACL shape validates the overall bounding box of the whole model (dataset).
1. geom:DatasetBBoxShape targets a single node, the graph IRI <https://vng.nl/geometries/> (sh:targetNode).
2. A SPARQL-based constraint (sh:sparql) runs one query for that node.
3. A subquery goes over all geometries that have geom:eastings, geom:northings and the six bbox properties (geom:bboxMinX/Y/Z and geom:bboxMaxX/Y/Z). It calculates the global extent:
   - X: min and max of (bbox X - eastings)
   - Y: min and max of (bbox Y - northings)
   - Z: min and max of the bbox Z values
   The eastings and northings are subtracted, so X and Y are relative to the model origin.
4. The model is reported as a violation when the total size of the extent is smaller than 1 or larger than 100 on any axis (for example, globalMaxX - globalMinX).
5. The result message lists the six global values ("Dataset BBox violation: globalMinX=..., globalMaxX=..., ...").
6. The severity is sh:Violation.
""" ;
    shacl:shapeUri "validate-model-bboxes.ttl" .